/-!
# Linear Noether normalization

Let `k` be an infinite field and `A` be a nontrivial commutative `k`-algebra generated by a finite
tuple `x₁, …, xₙ`. Nagata's Noether normalization (`exists_finite_inj_algHom_of_fg`) produces an
injective module-finite map `k[T₁, …, T_d] → A` over every field by nonlinear variable shifts
`Xᵢ ↦ Xᵢ + X₀ ^ rᵢ`, which destroy homogeneity in graded coordinate rings. Over an infinite field
one can instead choose parameters `yᵢ = ∑ⱼ Cᵢⱼ xⱼ` that are linear combinations of the prescribed
generators: `TauCeti.exists_linear_normalization` constructs `d ≤ n` and a `d × n` matrix `C` over
`k` such that `y` is algebraically independent over `k`, the evaluation map `k[T₁, …, T_d] → A` is
module-finite, and `ringKrullDim A = d`. Neither reducedness nor irreducibility of `A` is assumed.

The elimination step works over any commutative ring `R`. Given a relation `f(x) = 0` and a
coordinate `i : Fin (n + 1)` together with a shear direction `a : Fin n → R` on which the top
homogeneous component of `f` evaluates to a unit at `i.insertNth 1 a`, the sheared polynomial
`MvPolynomial.shearToPolynomial i a f` has degree at most `f.totalDegree` and unit coefficient in
that degree, making `x i` integral over the subalgebra generated by the sheared coordinates
`z j = x (i.succAbove j) - a j • x i` (`TauCeti.isIntegral_shear_of_isUnit_eval`). When `x`
generates `A` over `R`, `A` is module-finite over that subalgebra
(`TauCeti.finite_adjoin_shear_of_isUnit_eval`). Over an infinite domain, dehomogenization
injectivity and `MvPolynomial.funext` supply a direction where the top homogeneous part does not
vanish (`TauCeti.exists_eval_insertNth_homogeneousComponent_ne_zero`).

Because the parameters `yᵢ` are algebraically independent, the rows of `C` are linearly independent
(`AlgebraicIndependent.linearIndependent_of_sum_smul`). Under scalar extension to `S ⊗[R] A`,
module-finiteness of `MvPolynomial.aeval` persists unconditionally (`TauCeti.finite_aeval_one_tmul`)
and algebraic independence persists along any flat `R`-algebra `S`
(`AlgebraicIndependent.one_tmul`), so any linear normalization over a field persists after arbitrary
extension of the base field (`TauCeti.algebraicIndependent_and_finite_sum_smul_tmul`).

Finally, over `𝔽₂ = ZMod 2` the plane cubic union of three lines
`A = 𝔽₂[X, Y] ⧸ (X Y (X + Y))` admits a quadratic normalization `z = x² + x y + y²`
(`TauCeti.algebraicIndependent_and_finite_quadratic_zmod_two`), hence has Krull dimension `1`, yet
admits no linear normalization in the presentation `(x, y)`
(`TauCeti.not_exists_linear_normalization_zmod_two`), showing that the infinite-field hypothesis is
sharp.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.isIntegral_shear_of_isUnit_eval`: a polynomial relation `aeval x f = 0` whose top
  homogeneous part is a unit at `i.insertNth 1 a` makes `x i` integral over the `R`-subalgebra
  generated by `fun j ↦ x (i.succAbove j) - a j • x i`.
* `TauCeti.finite_adjoin_shear_of_isUnit_eval`: if in addition `x` generates `A` over `R`, then `A`
  is module-finite over that subalgebra.
* `TauCeti.exists_eval_insertNth_homogeneousComponent_ne_zero`: over an infinite domain, the top
  homogeneous component of any nonzero polynomial takes a nonzero value at `i.insertNth 1 a` for
  some `a`.
* `TauCeti.exists_linear_normalization`: linear Noether normalization for a generating tuple
  `x : Fin n → A` of a nontrivial algebra over an infinite field.
* `TauCeti.exists_linear_normalization_of_fintype`: linear Noether normalization for a generating
  family indexed by an arbitrary `Fintype`.
* `AlgebraicIndependent.linearIndependent_of_sum_smul`: if `i ↦ ∑ j, C i j • x j` is algebraically
  independent over `R`, the rows of `C` are `R`-linearly independent.
* `AlgebraicIndependent.one_tmul`: algebraic independence of `y` over `R` persists for `1 ⊗ₜ y`
  over any flat `R`-algebra `S`.
* `TauCeti.finite_aeval_one_tmul`: module-finiteness of `MvPolynomial.aeval y` persists for
  `1 ⊗ₜ y` over any commutative `R`-algebra `S`.
* `TauCeti.algebraicIndependent_and_finite_sum_smul_tmul`: a linear normalization persists under
  flat base change, in particular under any field extension.
* `TauCeti.algebraicIndependent_and_finite_quadratic_zmod_two`: `𝔽₂[X, Y] ⧸ (X Y (X + Y))` is
  module-finite over the algebraically independent quadratic element `x² + x y + y²`.
* `TauCeti.not_exists_linear_normalization_zmod_two`: `𝔽₂[X, Y] ⧸ (X Y (X + Y))` admits no linear
  Noether normalization in its coordinate generators, witnessing sharpness of `[Infinite k]`.

## References

* J. S. Milne, *Algebraic Geometry*, Lemma 2.43, Theorem 2.45, Lemma 2.46, and Remark 2.47.
* J. S. Milne, *Commutative Algebra*, Theorem 8.1 and Remark 8.4.
* [Stacks Project, Tag 00OW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00OW)
-/

